Phantom-WG Modern — Update Guide
==================================

Standard Update:
  ./tools/prod.sh update

  This pulls the latest release, syncs the images of the selected source and
  recreates all services. Environment files (.env, .env.daemon,
  .env.auth-service) and docker-compose.override.yml are always preserved.
  If an update stops halfway, run it again.

  A package installed from the release zip has no git history, so there is
  nothing to pull: the code comes from the new zip, and update applies it.

  update moves forward only. It compares the code version with the one this
  host last applied (container-data/.applied-version) and stops on an older
  package. To go back, follow Rollback below.

Local Changes:
  Server-specific changes (ports, resource limits, extra volumes) belong in
  docker-compose.override.yml. It is not tracked by git, so updates leave
  it as it is.

  docker-compose.yml comes with each release. An update stops if it has local
  changes: move them to the override, then discard them:

    git checkout -- docker-compose.yml

Dependency Updates:
  Every update syncs the images of the source selected in .env: the registry
  source pulls the images pinned by the release, the build source builds the
  Dockerfiles of the release, the archive source loads images/ of the package
  after checking it. To run this step alone:

    ./tools/prod.sh images sync

  To rebuild from scratch on the build source:

    ./tools/prod.sh rebuild
    ./tools/prod.sh up

Version Check:
  ./tools/prod.sh show-versions

  Shows the current daemon version and bridge versions running
  inside the container.

Rollback:
  To roll back to a previous version:

    git fetch --tags
    git checkout v2.0.0
    ./tools/prod.sh images sync
    ./tools/prod.sh up
    ./tools/prod.sh restart

  up applies the images and docker-compose.yml of that version, restart loads
  its code.

  This creates a detached HEAD state — you are pinned to that tag.
  To resume receiving updates, switch back to main:

    git checkout main
    ./tools/prod.sh update

  Environment files and runtime data are unaffected by rollback.

Hard Reset:
  ./tools/prod.sh hard-reset

  Destroys ALL data: secrets, auth database, client databases,
  and Docker volumes. Requires typing 'yes' to confirm. Environment files
  and docker-compose.override.yml stay. The daemon writes its data as root,
  so run it as root or with sudo.

  After hard reset, run setup again:
    ./tools/prod.sh setup

What Gets Preserved on Update:
  docker-compose.override.yml   Always preserved (not tracked by git)
  .env                          Always preserved (not tracked by git)
  .env.daemon                   Always preserved (not tracked by git)
  .env.auth-service             Always preserved (not tracked by git)
  container-data/               Always preserved (runtime data, not in git)

What Gets Updated:
  phantom_daemon/                      Daemon source code
  services/auth-service/               Auth service source
  services/react-spa/dist/             Web dashboard build
  services/nginx/                      Reverse proxy config
  tools/                               Production CLI, libraries and image pins
  docker-compose.yml                   Production stack
  docker-compose.override.yml.example  Override template
  Dockerfile, nginx.Dockerfile         Image definitions
  requirements.txt                     Python dependencies